\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.3}{\ignorespaces The RubricNet architecture. Each descriptor $x_i$ is scored independently by a two-parameter subnetwork $g_i$; the bounded scores are summed into the aggregated difficulty score $S(x)$, and an ordinal head maps $S(x)$ to $K$ cumulative class probabilities. No descriptor interacts with any other before the summation, so $g_i(x_i)$ is exactly descriptor $i$'s contribution to the prediction.}}{27}{figure.4.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:architecture}{{4.3}{27}{The RubricNet architecture. Each descriptor $x_i$ is scored independently by a two-parameter subnetwork $g_i$; the bounded scores are summed into the aggregated difficulty score $S(x)$, and an ordinal head maps $S(x)$ to $K$ cumulative class probabilities. No descriptor interacts with any other before the summation, so $g_i(x_i)$ is exactly descriptor $i$'s contribution to the prediction}{figure.4.3}{}}
